AI Story Writer Agent — Scaffold Plan

Context

The organization is building an AI PDLC pipeline: PRD Agent → Discovery Agent → AI Story Writer Agent. The Story Writer Agent takes refined PRDs (Markdown) and produces JIRA-ready Scrum artifacts (Epics → Stories → Sub-tasks). The user wants all three implementation approaches scaffolded in a single monorepo:

1. packages/skill — Claude Code Skill (publishable to org catalog)
2. packages/service — Standalone TypeScript service (deployable to GCP Cloud Run)
3. packages/hybrid — Core library + both wrappers

Key decisions already made:
- PRD input format: Markdown files
- JIRA structure: Scrum (Epics → Stories → Sub-tasks, Sprint-based)
- JIRA workflow: Review-first (generate preview → PO approves → push to JIRA)
- Cloud: GCP (Cloud Run, Firestore, Pub/Sub, Secret Manager)
- No local repo cloning — GitHub API/MCP/GraphQL only

